-- Backfills the email_* columns on project_contacts for 7 contacts added to
-- the "RevHub-Marketing" tab of Chad's RevHub Target Accounts sheet since the
-- last sync (HR Transformed, BleuBully Bedding x2, and Interplay Learning x4).
-- Matches by email address, case-insensitive. Only fills a column when it's
-- currently null, so this can never clobber a manual edit someone already
-- made in the app. Generated by the daily revhub-email-draft-sync task.

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$Building HR Transformed's next repeatable growth system$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Allyns,

I saw HR Transformed's search for fractional Chief Marketing and Growth leadership. What stood out is the breadth of the mandate: brand, acquisition, conversion, retention, B2B expansion, segmentation, attribution, dashboards, and revenue optimization. That is not simply a marketing hire. It is the buildout of a connected commercial growth system.

I have spent more than 15 years creating those systems across positioning, customer segmentation, demand generation, CRM, lifecycle orchestration, forecasting, analytics, and executive reporting. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while connecting fragmented CRM, marketing, customer, call-center, and operational data into one usable growth model. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I bring both the strategy and analytical depth needed to move quickly without requiring HR Transformed to assemble several separate specialists.

For HR Transformed, I would begin by identifying the highest-value client segments, sharpening the growth narrative for each, mapping the journey from awareness through consultation and recurring engagement, and establishing one measurement model for acquisition, conversion, retention, and expansion.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Allyns,

One practical first deliverable would be a commercial growth map connecting each priority client segment to its buying trigger, value proposition, entry channel, consultation path, service mix, retention signals, and expansion opportunities. That would make it easier to see where growth is constrained by audience, message, process, or measurement.

Would a brief conversation next week be worthwhile?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Allyns,

Closing the loop. HR Transformed already has strong credibility and client proof. The opportunity I see is turning that foundation into a more predictable system for demand, conversion, recurring engagement, and executive visibility.

I would be glad to share a concise first-30-days framework in 20 minutes. Is there a time worth holding?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Verified public business email published on HR Transformed's official website.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('allyns@hrtransformed.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$A commercial operating layer for BleuBully's next stage$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Amanda,

Your work taking BleuBully from a product idea to a sold-out D2C brand stood out. The next phase appears materially different from launch: product and color expansion, acquisition efficiency, website conversion, lifecycle growth, wholesale opportunities, inventory decisions, and a clearer view of contribution economics.

I have spent more than 15 years building commercial systems that connect customer segmentation, campaigns, CRM, lifecycle behavior, forecasting, analytics, and executive reporting. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while unifying fragmented customer, marketing, call-center, and operational data. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I add the strategy and analytical depth needed to turn growth activity into a shared operating model.

For BleuBully, a practical first step could connect audience and creative tests to first-order margin, product affinity, repeat purchase, wholesale potential, and inventory implications. That would help clarify which customer and channel patterns are worth scaling as the assortment expands.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation to compare approaches? Our framework is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Amanda,

One concrete deliverable could be a customer and channel growth map connecting acquisition source, creative message, first purchase, product mix, margin, repeat behavior, and wholesale potential. It would show where BleuBully is generating durable customer value versus short-term demand.

Would a brief conversation next week be useful?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Amanda,

Closing the loop. BleuBully already has the brand story and early market proof. The opportunity I see is building the commercial measurement and decision system that helps the team scale acquisition, retention, assortment, and wholesale from the same evidence.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is another stakeholder closer to that work?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Verified public business email published by Amanda Pond in a LinkedIn post for MOD Consulting. This is Amanda's consulting-company address, not a BleuBully company-domain email.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('amanda@modconsultingco.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$A faster path to Interplay's revenue source of truth$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi John,

I saw Interplay Learning's search for its first dedicated Senior Director of Revenue Operations. The mandate is substantial: create one source of truth across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, and Finance, strengthen forecasting, govern Salesforce and the broader GTM stack, and establish the operating cadence behind the full revenue lifecycle.

That work is closely aligned with the commercial systems I have spent more than 15 years building. At QXO, I helped connect fragmented CRM, marketing automation, customer, credit, call-center, and operational data while scaling digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I combine commercial architecture, data strategy, forecasting, analytics, and hands-on implementation.

For Interplay, a focused first phase could establish the lifecycle definitions, source-of-truth metrics, forecast inputs, systems ownership, dashboard requirements, and decision rules the new RevOps leader should inherit. That would reduce discovery time and create earlier value across the software, training-services, and customer lifecycle.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? Our approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi John,

One practical deliverable would be a revenue architecture connecting acquisition, qualification, pipeline, delivery, product adoption, customer health, retention, expansion, and financial planning. It would identify where Interplay's current visibility is limited by data, definitions, process, or ownership and give the internal hire a sequenced roadmap.

Would a brief conversation next week be worthwhile?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi John,

Closing the loop. The opportunity I see is helping Interplay establish the commercial operating model before the new RevOps leader has to discover and reconcile every dependency independently.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is another executive closer to the initial architecture work?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by the verified public address ddonovan@interplaylearning.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('jpumpelly@interplaylearning.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$Connecting Interplay's growth engine after ITI$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Doug,

Interplay's expansion across immersive skilled-trades training, AI-enabled learning, and the Industrial Training International portfolio creates a meaningful growth opportunity, but also a more complex commercial operating model. The current search for Interplay's first dedicated Senior Director of Revenue Operations suggests the company is ready to connect that growth through one view of customers, pipeline, delivery, engagement, retention, expansion, and forecasting.

I have spent more than 15 years building those systems. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while connecting fragmented CRM, marketing, customer, credit, call-center, and operational data. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I combine commercial strategy, data architecture, forecasting, analytics, and implementation capacity.

For Interplay, an initial engagement could define the executive decision model behind the RevOps build: the customer and portfolio segments that matter most, the lifecycle and source-of-truth measures beneath them, and the operating cadence needed to turn insight into action. That would help the internal leader create value earlier while reducing the burden of discovering every dependency from scratch.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? Our approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Doug,

One concrete deliverable could be an executive growth map connecting Interplay's market segments and product portfolio to acquisition, sales conversion, implementation, learner engagement, customer value, retention, expansion, and contribution economics. It would help leadership see where the ITI integration and broader platform are creating leverage and where operating constraints need attention.

Would a brief conversation next week be useful?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Doug,

Closing the loop. Interplay already has differentiated technology, content, and customer impact. The opportunity I see is building the commercial decision system that helps leadership scale those assets through the same evidence.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Verified public business email published by Doug Donovan in a public LinkedIn reply.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('ddonovan@interplaylearning.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$From marketing activity to Interplay revenue visibility$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Emma,

Interplay's search for its first dedicated Senior Director of Revenue Operations caught my attention because the value of that role will depend heavily on how Marketing and RevOps define the customer lifecycle together. The challenge is not simply better attribution. It is connecting audience strategy, campaigns, CRM stages, pipeline, implementation, learner engagement, retention, and expansion through one trusted model.

I have spent more than 15 years building that connective layer. At QXO, I helped scale digital revenue from $400M to $1.25B while joining fragmented CRM, marketing automation, customer, call-center, and operational data. Through RevHub, my partner Harsh and I provide commercial architecture, analytics, forecasting, and implementation capacity.

For Interplay, a useful first step could be a multi-audience growth map across employers, education partners, workforce organizations, and skilled-trades learners, with shared definitions for buying triggers, campaign sources, qualification, pipeline, adoption, renewal, and expansion.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation to compare approaches? Our framework is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Emma,

One practical deliverable would be a marketing-to-revenue measurement architecture connecting segment, message, source, campaign, CRM stage, opportunity quality, product engagement, retention, and expansion. It would help the team distinguish activity that creates durable customer value from activity that only produces surface-level volume.

Would a brief discussion next week be worthwhile?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Emma,

Closing the loop. I believe Interplay's RevOps build creates a strong opportunity for Marketing to establish shared lifecycle and value definitions before the systems and dashboards become fixed.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is another leader closer to that work?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by the verified public address ddonovan@interplaylearning.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('evas@interplaylearning.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$Connecting Interplay adoption, retention, and expansion$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Heather,

Interplay's search for its first dedicated Senior Director of Revenue Operations caught my attention because the role will only create value if the customer lifecycle is represented as clearly as pipeline and bookings. Your Customer Success and Services mandate sits at the center of implementation, adoption, learner and administrator engagement, service demand, renewal, and expansion.

