For Interplay, a practical first step could define the customer-value model behind the RevOps build: implementation milestones, engagement signals, customer-health rules, renewal risk, expansion potential, ownership, and the forecast implications of each stage.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation to compare approaches? Our framework is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Heather,

One concrete deliverable could be a customer lifecycle and health architecture connecting implementation, usage, service demand, stakeholder adoption, renewal, expansion, and forecast confidence. It would help Customer Success, Revenue, and Finance prioritize accounts using shared evidence.

Would a brief conversation next week be useful?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Heather,

Closing the loop. The opportunity I see is ensuring Interplay's new revenue operating model captures customer value and risk, not only pre-sale activity.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding, or is another executive closer to the initial customer-lifecycle design?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Assumed from the first-initial-plus-last-name pattern demonstrated by the verified public address ddonovan@interplaylearning.com. This email may not work and should be verified before sending.$$)
where lower(email) = lower('hgranato@interplaylearning.com');

update public.project_contacts
set
  email_subject = coalesce(email_subject, $$Connecting BleuBully's media momentum to measurable growth$$),
  email_intro_message = coalesce(email_intro_message, $$Hi Kelsey,

I saw BleuBully's search for fractional CMO leadership and your work building the brand's press visibility. The company now has strong proof points, including product awards, founder coverage, a clear giveback mission, and an expanding assortment. The next opportunity is making sure that communications momentum connects to audience growth, ecommerce conversion, retention, wholesale conversations, and measurable revenue.

I have spent more than 15 years building commercial systems that connect segmentation, positioning, campaign execution, CRM, lifecycle programs, analytics, and executive reporting. Through RevHub, my partner and I add both strategic leadership and hands-on analytical capacity.

For BleuBully, a useful first phase could connect founder and product narratives, priority audiences, media and content calendars, campaign activation, ecommerce and CRM signals, wholesale interest, and one shared performance scorecard.

Would you be open to a 20-minute conversation next week? My approach is here: https://www.aboutchad.com/approach

Best,
Chad Parker$$),
  email_follow_up_1 = coalesce(email_follow_up_1, $$Hi Kelsey,

One practical deliverable could be a communications-to-growth map showing which audiences matter, which founder and product stories should lead, how media coverage is activated across owned channels, and how engagement connects to customer acquisition, retention, and wholesale interest.

Would a brief conversation next week be worthwhile?$$),
  email_follow_up_2 = coalesce(email_follow_up_2, $$Hi Kelsey,

Closing the loop. The opportunity I see is helping BleuBully turn strong press and brand credibility into a repeatable commercial system with clearer audience priorities, activation paths, and revenue evidence.

Is there a 20-minute window worth holding?$$),
  email_assumption_notice = coalesce(email_assumption_notice, $$Verified public business email published on BleuBully Bedding's official website for PR and press inquiries.$$)
